      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "he plan correctly identifies 1870, 1880, and 1900 as the target census years and correctly notes that the 1890 census is unavailable. The main issue is persistence: although the narrative and research_append call describe six plan items (pli_007–pli_012), the file changes summary confirms only the first three items (pli_007–pli_009). This creates uncertainty about whether the three Ancestry fallback items were actually persisted."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_research_plan_011",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Completeness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The plan itself is complete in concept because it contains three FamilySearch searches and three Ancestry fallback searches. However, the persisted artifact does not clearly confirm that all six items were successfully written. The discrepancy between the six items described in the plan and the three items shown in the file-change summary prevents full confidence in the completeness of the saved research plan."
    },
